2. Structure of a Typical Mobile App Team

A typical mobile application team can be structured like this:

                    PRODUCT MANAGER
                          |
                          |
             ---------------------------
             |            |            |
          DESIGNER    MOBILE DEV    BACKEND/API DEV
             |            |            |
             |            |            |
             ----------- TESTER --------
                          |
                          |
                     Final App

Role of each team member:

   1. Product Manager: Decides what features should be built, prepares requirements, and coordinates the team.
   2. Designer: Creates the UI/UX design, wireframes, colors, screens, and user flow.
   3. Mobile Developer: Converts the designs into a working mobile application using Flutter/Dart.
   4. Backend/API Developer: Creates APIs, database logic, authentication, and server-side functionality.
   5. Tester/QA: Tests the application, finds bugs, and checks whether the feature works correctly.
